; The expansion backtrace (macro-system.md MAC-DIAG-4). A diagnostic
; arising INSIDE an expansion anchors at the invocation, in this file -
; that much was always true - and since 2026-08-14 it also carries one
; `&` frame per enclosing instantiation, naming the macro with the span
; of its DECLARATION in ITS OWN file: the two-source diagnostic the
; one-unit `Diag` could not express while a frame was a bare string.
;
;   (frameBad 1)    one frame - `frameBad`, declared in MacFrame.ax
;   (frameOuter 2)  two frames, outermost first: `frameOuter` invoked
;                   here, whose template invoked `frameBad`
;
; Until then this file's two AX3001s rendered with no mention of any
; macro: an error about a name that appears nowhere on the line it
; points at.
(import MacFrame)

(:: one (-> Int Int))

(fn (one n) (frameBad n))

(:: two (-> Int Int))

(fn (two n) (frameOuter n))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ (one 1) (two 2)))
